From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandre Derumier <aderumier@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:20:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] qasf: Let the renderers pace the samples.

With a graph clock, the ASF reader let the WM async reader pace the
samples on its own clock, handing each one over at its presentation
time: a sample delayed once (the reader's clock started before the
graph ran, a busy delivery thread) reached the renderer late, and the
reader never got ahead again. A renderer dropping the samples reaching
it past their time then showed none.

Deliver the samples as soon as they are read, as without a clock: the
renderers wait for their presentation time themselves, blocking in
Receive().

Game impacted: Hatsune Miku Project DIVA Arcade (Sega RingEdge 2): its
video renderer queues up to 5 frames and drops those whose end time has
passed. With patch 0120 alone its WMV3 60 fps attract movie still froze
after a few seconds in some runs (its video 0.6 s late after a hiccup at
the start); with this patch it plays through every time.
---
--- a/dlls/qasf/asfreader.c
+++ b/dlls/qasf/asfreader.c
@@ -664,13 +664,13 @@
             filter->stream_count, stream_numbers, selections)))
         WARN("Failed to set reader %p stream selection, hr %#lx\n", filter->reader, hr);
 
-    if (SUCCEEDED(hr) && FAILED(hr = IWMReaderAdvanced2_SetUserProvidedClock(reader_advanced, !filter->filter.clock)))
+    /* Deliver the samples as soon as they are read, as without a clock: the
+     * renderers wait for their presentation time themselves (blocking in
+     * Receive()), and some drop the samples reaching them past it. */
+    if (SUCCEEDED(hr) && FAILED(hr = IWMReaderAdvanced2_SetUserProvidedClock(reader_advanced, TRUE)))
         WARN("Failed to set user provided clock, hr %#lx\n", hr);
-    else if (!filter->filter.clock)
-    {
-        if (SUCCEEDED(hr) && FAILED(hr = IWMReaderAdvanced2_DeliverTime(reader_advanced, -1)))
-            WARN("Failed to set user time, hr %#lx\n", hr);
-    }
+    else if (SUCCEEDED(hr) && FAILED(hr = IWMReaderAdvanced2_DeliverTime(reader_advanced, -1)))
+        WARN("Failed to set user time, hr %#lx\n", hr);
 
     IWMReaderAdvanced2_Release(reader_advanced);
 
